        "original_id": "d65163c7-25f0-5d02-8cb7-ce6525bc3384",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Der Freischütz, Il trovatore, Magic Hunter\n- People: Carl Maria von Weber, Friedrich Kind, Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez, Ildikó Enyedi\n- Topics: Opera, film adaptations, librettos\n\nFacts:\n- Der Freischütz, Op. 77, J. 277, is a German opera with spoken dialogue in three acts by Carl Maria von Weber and a libretto by Friedrich Kind.\n- Der Freischütz is usually translated as \"The Marksman\" or \"The Freeshooter.\"\n- Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the 1836 play El trovador.\n- Il trovatore is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano and based on Antonio García Gutiérrez's play El trovador.\n- Magic Hunter is a 1994 Hungarian-Swiss-French fantasy film written and directed by Ildikó Enyedi.\n- Magic Hunter is loosely inspired by the opera Der Freischütz and is titled Bűvös vadász in Hungarian and Freischütz in French.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
